{
 "study": "docs/research/MEMORY_LOADING.md",
 "increment": "ml-m5d",
 "previous": "ml-m5c",
 "phase": "M5d: the mixer reads PCM through the buffer's address, mono read once per frame",
 "change": "OriginalMacSoundEffects: RawPCM8/RawPCM16 readers (base.load / Int16(littleEndian: loadUnaligned), the backend's expressions) used inside withUnsafeBytes where inBounds holds (step >= 0 and, when looping, step < count; otherwise the bounds-checked M5c readers); a mono voice reads each frame once for both channels. New test: 1-3 frame buffers with steps of 1 and 2 (both paths), partial trailing frames, a move to exactly the end.",
 "profile": "Mixer benchmark (scratchpad mixbench; 8 voices, output 48 kHz, outputs hashed bit for bit): A12 ns per voice-frame, 192-frame callback: floats before M5c 37.20, M5c 48.72, raw 42.75, raw+mono 36.20 (960 frames: 34.67, 47.09, 41.08, 34.57); Mac 1.67, 2.82, 1.96, 1.60. In play (gate phone A/B, sounds mixed): AudioTrack thread 1.03-1.07 against 1.12 ms per tick.",
 "review": "Independent read-only review: one low-severity defect (a negative step, unreachable from the hosts, would have taken the raw path where the array readers trapped) fixed before the gate (step >= 0); memory safety for step >= 0 proved (Sterbenz on the wrap), bit identity and the fallback confirmed.",
 "notes": "First gate with frame-time windows (--ticks 600,1500) and sounds mixed (--sounds). Phone load: M5d 5.60-8.09 s (first run 8.09 with a 3.13 s read-ahead wait) against M5c 5.18-5.20; a 4+4 A/B with sounds (ml-m5d-snd) and a 3+3 muted control (ml-m5d-mute, where the mixer never runs) overlap once each sequence's first run is set aside (5.42-5.86 against 5.27-5.86; 5.53-5.66 against 5.36-5.65): the first run of a sequence waits longest for the read-ahead (3.13, 1.44, 1.40 s, M5d first each time), an order effect; launch to loaded 12.38-12.64 against 12.48-12.76 s. Frame time: main 10.27-10.38 against 10.35-10.43, render 6.93-7.09 against 7.08-7.67, process 25.89-26.59 against 26.62-27.30 ms per tick.",
